                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "43b167b5-9354-39d5-a0b9-8f2babbcde51",
                                        "entry_id": "db4d3a72-d400-3332-8c5a-58f6fd212825",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The simplest carboxylic acid, HCOOH, a colourless, corrosive liquid with a sharp odour systematically known as methanoic acid; it is present in the stings of ants, bees and nettles, and is prepared industrially by the oxidation of methanol or formaldehyde; it has some industrial uses, and its esters, the formates are used in perfumes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e4a49090-64c1-4c97-a7af-97c77dac1c1f",
                                                "sense_id": "43b167b5-9354-39d5-a0b9-8f2babbcde51",
                                                "text": "The ant has made himself illustrious / Through constant industry industrious. / So what? / Would you be calm and placid / If you were full of formic acid?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
